  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: The coastal flood risk will linger through mid- \nweek.\n\nCoastal flooding concerns continue across the region heading \ninto the new week in the wake of a departing nor'easter. While \nwind direction may be less favorable than this weekend, still \nexpect astro tides to remain elevated given the recent full \nmoon. This will result minor (to possibly moderate) coastal \nflooding with each high tide cycle (especially for the \nCharleston Harbor). \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Rising temperatures into mid week, remaining \nabove normal through the remainder of the week. \n\nUpper level ridging will build into the region through mid-\nweek. Today will be slightly warmer than the weekend with highs \nin the mid-80s. Clear skies and light to calm winds will likely \nresult in radiational cooling tonight with lows in the upper 50s\ninland and lower 60s across the coastal counties. As high \npressure builds over the region this week the forecast will \nlikely remain rain-free and feature a warming trend in \ntemperatures. The next chance of rain will be late week and into\nthe weekend.",
